{"content_id":"CL-LTG-HR07-DMX-001","domain_id_primary":"D-LTG","domain_ids_secondary":["D-EVD"],"content_type":"claim","route_file":"courses/pathway-lighting-02-production-flow.html","source_data_file":"scripts/course-data-lighting.mjs","course_id":"C-LTG-PRODUCTION-FLOW","tier_learning":"T4","responsibility_band":"R2","authority_class":"A0","module_identifier":"System Architecture","lesson_identifier":"Lighting Control & Data","block_identifier":"quiz-glossary-dmx-universe","question_identifier":"Q-LTG-HR07-DMX-001","visual_identifier":null,"learner_facing_text":"A DMX universe is a control-data grouping containing up to 512 DMX data slots; it is not the number of fixtures on the rig.","content_classification":"external_fact","safety_criticality":"low","authority_implication":"system_reasoning","publication_state":"noindex_review","supersedes_content_id":null,"superseded_by_content_id":null,"last_content_reviewed_at":"2026-08-31","notes":"Current E1.11 packet structure includes a START Code plus up to 512 following data slots. Learner wording intentionally uses 'data slots' rather than fixture count."}
{"content_id":"Q-LTG-HR07-DMX-001","domain_id_primary":"D-LTG","domain_ids_secondary":["D-EVD"],"content_type":"question","route_file":"courses/pathway-lighting-02-production-flow.html","source_data_file":"scripts/course-data-lighting.mjs","course_id":"C-LTG-PRODUCTION-FLOW","tier_learning":"T4","responsibility_band":"R2","authority_class":"A0","module_identifier":"System Architecture","lesson_identifier":"Lighting Control & Data","block_identifier":"quiz","question_identifier":"Q-LTG-HR07-DMX-001","visual_identifier":null,"learner_facing_text":"What is a DMX universe? Correct answer: A set of up to 512 DMX data slots.","content_classification":"assessment_prompt","safety_criticality":"low","authority_implication":"system_reasoning","publication_state":"noindex_review","supersedes_content_id":null,"superseded_by_content_id":null,"last_content_reviewed_at":"2026-08-31","notes":"Existing learner-facing scored question normalized into the assessment lineage model."}
{"content_id":"QR-Q-LTG-HR07-DMX-001","domain_id_primary":"D-LTG","domain_ids_secondary":["D-EVD"],"content_type":"answer_rationale","route_file":"courses/pathway-lighting-02-production-flow.html","source_data_file":"scripts/course-data-lighting.mjs","course_id":"C-LTG-PRODUCTION-FLOW","tier_learning":"T4","responsibility_band":"R2","authority_class":"A0","module_identifier":"System Architecture","lesson_identifier":"Lighting Control & Data","block_identifier":"quiz-coaching","question_identifier":"Q-LTG-HR07-DMX-001","visual_identifier":null,"learner_facing_text":"A DMX universe is a control-data grouping, not a fixture count; fixtures consume one or more slots according to their control mode.","content_classification":"source_backed_instruction","safety_criticality":"low","authority_implication":"system_reasoning","publication_state":"noindex_review","supersedes_content_id":null,"superseded_by_content_id":null,"last_content_reviewed_at":"2026-08-31","notes":"Rationale is traced to CL-LTG-HR07-DMX-001."}
{"content_id":"CL-LTG-HR07-RDM-001","domain_id_primary":"D-LTG","domain_ids_secondary":[],"content_type":"claim","route_file":"courses/pathway-lighting-02-production-flow.html","source_data_file":"scripts/course-data-lighting.mjs","course_id":"C-LTG-PRODUCTION-FLOW","tier_learning":"T4","responsibility_band":"R2","authority_class":"A0","module_identifier":"System Architecture","lesson_identifier":"Lighting Control & Data","block_identifier":"glossary-rdm","question_identifier":null,"visual_identifier":null,"learner_facing_text":"RDM provides bidirectional management over compatible DMX512 infrastructure, including device discovery and supported remote configuration/status functions.","content_classification":"external_fact","safety_criticality":"low","authority_implication":"system_reasoning","publication_state":"noindex_review","supersedes_content_id":null,"superseded_by_content_id":null,"last_content_reviewed_at":"2026-08-31","notes":"High-level concept only; product-specific RDM behavior and management permissions depend on the actual system."}
{"content_id":"CL-LTG-HR07-SACN-001","domain_id_primary":"D-LTG","domain_ids_secondary":[],"content_type":"claim","route_file":"courses/pathway-lighting-02-production-flow.html","source_data_file":"scripts/course-data-lighting.mjs","course_id":"C-LTG-PRODUCTION-FLOW","tier_learning":"T4","responsibility_band":"R2","authority_class":"A0","module_identifier":"System Architecture","lesson_identifier":"Lighting Control & Data","block_identifier":"glossary-sacn","question_identifier":null,"visual_identifier":null,"learner_facing_text":"sACN (ANSI E1.31) is a standardized IP-network transport for DMX512A data and includes defined data addressing and network-management behavior.","content_classification":"external_fact","safety_criticality":"low","authority_implication":"system_reasoning","publication_state":"noindex_review","supersedes_content_id":null,"superseded_by_content_id":null,"last_content_reviewed_at":"2026-08-31","notes":"Current standard is ANSI E1.31-2025, published January 5, 2026, with IPv4 and IPv6 support."}
{"content_id":"CL-LTG-HR07-ARTNET-001","domain_id_primary":"D-LTG","domain_ids_secondary":[],"content_type":"claim","route_file":"courses/pathway-lighting-02-production-flow.html","source_data_file":"scripts/course-data-lighting.mjs","course_id":"C-LTG-PRODUCTION-FLOW","tier_learning":"T4","responsibility_band":"R2","authority_class":"A0","module_identifier":"System Architecture","lesson_identifier":"Lighting Control & Data","block_identifier":"glossary-artnet","question_identifier":null,"visual_identifier":null,"learner_facing_text":"Art-Net 4 is an Ethernet/IP-based entertainment-control protocol used to transport DMX512 data and related lighting-control information across a network.","content_classification":"external_fact","safety_criticality":"low","authority_implication":"system_reasoning","publication_state":"noindex_review","supersedes_content_id":null,"superseded_by_content_id":null,"last_content_reviewed_at":"2026-08-31","notes":"Art-Net is vendor-owned by Artistic Licence but published for royalty-free use subject to its conditions."}
{"content_id":"CL-LTG-HR07-FLOW-001","domain_id_primary":"D-LTG","domain_ids_secondary":[],"content_type":"claim","route_file":"courses/pathway-lighting-02-production-flow.html","source_data_file":"scripts/course-data-lighting.mjs","course_id":"C-LTG-PRODUCTION-FLOW","tier_learning":"T4","responsibility_band":"R2","authority_class":"A0","module_identifier":"System Architecture","lesson_identifier":"Lighting Control & Data","block_identifier":"control-path-example","question_identifier":null,"visual_identifier":null,"learner_facing_text":"A common lighting-control architecture can pass from an operator/console through Ethernet or other data transport to gateways/nodes and then into DMX/device-level control before reaching fixtures or other endpoints.","content_classification":"cross_source_pattern","safety_criticality":"low","authority_implication":"system_reasoning","publication_state":"noindex_review","supersedes_content_id":null,"superseded_by_content_id":null,"last_content_reviewed_at":"2026-08-31","notes":"Example architecture, not a universal required topology. Systems can differ materially by product, venue and protocol design."}
{"content_id":"CL-LTG-HR07-NETWORK-001","domain_id_primary":"D-LTG","domain_ids_secondary":["D-EVD"],"content_type":"claim","route_file":"courses/pathway-lighting-02-production-flow.html","source_data_file":"scripts/course-data-lighting.mjs","course_id":"C-LTG-PRODUCTION-FLOW","tier_learning":"T4","responsibility_band":"R2","authority_class":"A0","module_identifier":"System Architecture","lesson_identifier":"Lighting Control & Data","block_identifier":"beginner-mistakes-network","question_identifier":null,"visual_identifier":null,"learner_facing_text":"A physically connected Ethernet path does not by itself prove a lighting-control network is logically correct; addressing, universe mapping/routing, casting/priority/merging behavior and the configured network architecture can affect operation.","content_classification":"cross_source_pattern","safety_criticality":"moderate","authority_implication":"system_reasoning","publication_state":"noindex_review","supersedes_content_id":null,"superseded_by_content_id":null,"last_content_reviewed_at":"2026-08-31","notes":"Current page also names VLANs and switch configuration. Those are legitimate network-design variables but are not mandated by E1.31 itself; retain practitioner/vendor qualification before stronger wording."}
{"content_id":"CL-LTG-HR07-C3-BOUNDARY-001","domain_id_primary":"D-LTG","domain_ids_secondary":["D-ELC","D-RIG","D-EVD"],"content_type":"boundary","route_file":"courses/pathway-lighting-03-system-design.html","source_data_file":"scripts/course-data-advanced.mjs","course_id":"C-LTG-SYSTEM-DESIGN","tier_learning":"T7","responsibility_band":"R5","authority_class":"A0","module_identifier":"Protocols & Networked Control","lesson_identifier":"Build the Control Path in Layers","block_identifier":"stop-authority","question_identifier":null,"visual_identifier":null,"learner_facing_text":"Protocol and architecture literacy does not by itself authorize product-specific network configuration, venue-infrastructure changes, energized electrical work, rigging decisions, or employer appointment as a lighting systems designer.","content_classification":"safety_boundary","safety_criticality":"high","authority_implication":"specialist_external","publication_state":"noindex_review","supersedes_content_id":null,"superseded_by_content_id":null,"last_content_reviewed_at":"2026-08-31","notes":"Internal authority boundary supported by HR-01/HR-02 external gates and lighting research architecture."}
